{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): I've done her observations. Blood pressure was one forty over ninety-two, no, sorry, I did it again, one thirty-two over eighty-four. Pulse is ninety-six, sats ninety-eight percent.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Lovely, thank you. Come on in, both of you, have a seat. What's been wearing you out?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): I'm shattered, that's the main thing. And the periods, they're ridiculous. I'm sick of people asking if I'm alright.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Fair enough. When you say shattered, is it that you can't get going, or you're sleepy, or both?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Can't get going. I sleep and I wake up just as done in. And my hair's falling out in clumps in the shower.",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (CAREGIVER): The plughole's full of it. I've been coming round most days. She lives on her own and the shopping was getting left.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): That sounds exhausting. Any breathlessness mixed in with the tiredness?",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): Not on the stairs, or walking to the shop?",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (PATIENT): Well, actually, the stairs, yes. I stop halfway and sit. I just meant I'm not gasping while I'm sat here. Don't put words in my mouth.",
  "[SEG0011] person_4 (CAREGIVER): She does sit on the landing. I've watched her do it.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Noted, thank you. Tell me about the periods, in your own words.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): They're a nightmare. Flooding. It's been six months. No, hang on, a year. Since last spring, a full year.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): A year, right. How many pads would you get through on a heavy day?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): I don't count them. Loads. A pack doesn't last. Maybe eight, maybe more, I don't know, I just keep changing.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): And clots?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah. Big ones. Size of a fifty pence, sometimes bigger, I can't really say. It's grim.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain with the breathlessness, or palpitations, your heart racing?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): No chest pain. Heart's not racing. I'm just puffed and tired.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Dizziness, or fainting?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): No. Bit light-headed if I stand up quick, but I haven't fainted. Wait, is light-headed the same? I said no. Ignore that. No fainting, and I'm not dizzy really. Just the odd head rush.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever, or a cough?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Her mum's got an underactive thyroid, by the way. I don't know if that matters. She's been on thyroxine for years.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Useful to know, thank you. Have you yourself ever been told your thyroid was off, or that you were anaemic?",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (PATIENT): Thyroid, no. They did say I was anaemic, last year, at the surgery. That's why the iron.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): And the iron, what are you actually taking?",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (PATIENT): Those red iron tablets. Sometimes. When I remember. The box says three hundred milligrams.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (NURSE): Sorry, the list we've got says ferrous sulphate two hundred milligrams once a day. That's what's on the repeat.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (PATIENT): Well the box doesn't say that. I'm not making it up. And I don't take them every day, before you start.",
  "[SEG0031] person_4 (CAREGIVER): She leaves them in the cupboard. I've seen the packet barely touched.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Did they give you anything else for the bleeding?",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (PATIENT): Cyclokapron. I took it, then I stopped. And they wrote me a prescription for the mini pill, desogestrel, but I never even started that. Didn't fancy it.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): When did you stop the Cyclokapron?",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): March. No, April. After Easter. It made me feel sick anyway.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): And the hair, when did that start coming out?",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (PATIENT): No idea. Could've been months. I only noticed when the drain blocked. Don't ask me for a date.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (DOCTOR): That's alright, we don't need an exact day. Can I have a quick look at your hands and listen to your chest?",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (PATIENT): If you have to.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): Palms are pale, and the nail beds too. Chest is clear, no wheeze, good air entry.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): I think the tiredness and the puffing on the stairs are quite likely down to the anaemia from these heavy periods. I can't say that for certain until the bloods are back.",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (PATIENT): So more blood tests. Brilliant.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (DOCTOR): Yes. I'll request a full blood count and a ferritin, and thyroid function as well, given your mum's history and how washed out you are. Those will be today if the phlebotomy queue isn't awful.",
  "[SEG0044] person_4 (CAREGIVER): And a scan? Someone at the surgery mentioned a scan of the womb.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (DOCTOR): Maybe. If the bleeding carries on like this, or the bloods don't explain it, we might arrange a pelvic ultrasound. I won't book it today.",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (PATIENT): Fine. I'm not sitting in another waiting room for nothing.",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (DOCTOR): On the iron, I'd like you to take it every day rather than now and again, with a glass of orange juice if you can stomach it, and not with tea. We'll sort the exact tablet once we know which strength you've actually got at home. Bring the box next time.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (DOCTOR): Come back in two weeks and we'll go through the results. If the flooding gets worse or you can't manage the stairs at all, ring the surgery before then.",
  "[SEG0049] person_3 (PATIENT): Two weeks. Alright. Can we go? I'm done in.",
  "[SEG0050] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I'll bring the iron box. And I'll make sure she actually rings if she's worse.",
  "[SEG0051] person_2 (DOCTOR): That would help, thank you both. Take care on the way out."
 ],
